{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"intermediate/harness-engineering","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Harness Engineering","words":1604,"objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Explain why instructions alone cannot guarantee what an AI does","Say what an agent harness is, with the car, track and barriers picture","Name the four questions: what to say, what it sees, what world to build, and when it runs again"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[{"key":"intermediate/coding-agents","number":11,"title":"Code Agents","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"intermediate/agents-in-practice","number":12,"title":"Agents in Practice","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","number":14,"title":"Loop Engineering","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"the-problem-prompts-do-not-solve","text":"The Problem Prompts Do Not Solve","depth":2},{"id":"what-an-agent-harness-is","text":"What an Agent Harness is","depth":2},{"id":"four-disciplines-four-questions","text":"Four Disciplines, Four Questions","depth":2},{"id":"what-a-harness-is-made-of","text":"What a Harness is Made Of","depth":2},{"id":"some-actual-examples","text":"Some Actual Examples","depth":2},{"id":"no-harness-is-best-for-every-model","text":"No Harness is Best for Every Model","depth":2},{"id":"the-harnesses-are-open-now","text":"The Harnesses are Open Now","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"-articles","text":"📄 Articles","depth":3},{"id":"-videos","text":"🎬 Videos","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ended with hooks, and hooks were different from everything else in that module. Everything else is advice that the AI usually follows. A hook runs whether the AI wants it to or not. That difference is what this whole module is about."}],"lead":true},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"When a company lets an AI work with real data, real money or real customers, \"it usually behaves\" is not enough for some rules. This module explains how those rules are made safe, and why the same AI model can do very well in one product and badly in another."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-problem-prompts-do-not-solve","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Problem Prompts Do Not Solve"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An AI does not do exactly the same thing every time. Give it the same input twice, and you can get two different answers. In technical words, it is "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"non-deterministic"}]},{"type":"text","text":". And an agent that works for two hours makes thousands of small decisions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"So asking nicely never gives you a guarantee, no matter how often you ask. Say the AI must never send an email to a customer without a person's approval. You can write \"never send an email without approval\" in its instructions. That works most of the time. But for this rule, most of the time is not good enough. You need something built into the surroundings that behaves the same way every time, whatever the AI decides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Designing those surroundings is "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"harness engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"image","number":"13.1","title":"Prompt, context and harness on one drawing","note":"The engine is the prompt: it makes the power. The car is the context: the body built around the engine. The track and the barriers are the harness. The barriers do not steer. They do not make the car go the right way. They make it impossible to go the wrong way.","src":"course-images/intermediate/car-analogy.webp","alt":"Prompt, context and harness on one drawing","width":1270,"height":684},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The next two modules use this car picture again, so keep it in mind."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-an-agent-harness-is","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What an Agent Harness is"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The result of harness engineering is called an "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"agent harness"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the AI model, plus everything built around it, plus the place where it works."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LangChain says it in one line: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent = Model + Harness."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The model brings the intelligence. The harness turns that intelligence into useful, safe work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Think of a new employee. They are smart (that is the model). But the office, the procedures, the access cards, the forms that will not submit without a signature, and the manager's sign-off decide what they can actually do safely (that is the harness)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This also means the AI products you use are harnesses. Claude Code is a harness. Codex is a harness. Neither of them is a model. Put a different model inside, and less changes than you would expect."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The harness is the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"outer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" layer. It does not replace prompt and context work; it contains it."}]},{"type":"image","number":"13.2","title":"Prompt, context and harness as three layers","note":"Each ring contains the one inside it. That is why these are never alternatives. The harness writes the system prompt, summarises the chat and sends the helpers, so your context work happens inside the harness you picked.","src":"course-images/intermediate/onion-model.webp","alt":"Prompt, context and harness as three layers","width":1069,"height":697},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"four-disciplines-four-questions","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Four Disciplines, Four Questions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"By 2026, this work has split into four jobs, and each asks one plain question."}]},{"type":"image","number":"13.3","title":"What to say, what to see, and the world to build","note":"Read it from the bottom up. Each layer contains the one below it. At the bottom, a person talks to the robot. At the top, the person builds the place where the robot works.","src":"course-images/intermediate/prompt-vs-context-vs-harness.webp","alt":"What to say, what to see, and the world to build","width":1536,"height":1024},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Prompt engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what do I say, and how?"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Context engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what does the AI see in its chat?"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what world do I build around the AI?"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Loop engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": who decides when it runs again, and when it stops? That is the next module."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-harness-is-made-of","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What a Harness is Made Of"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"13.4","title":"What a Harness is Made Of","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/a09fe264790f2ffe29ead0217d80681b.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/1b1463e924a408e8baf487664bafd762.svg"}},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"In plain words: the instructions the AI reads first, the tools it can use (and their descriptions), the place it works in (its files, a safe practice area, a browser), the logic that hands work to helpers, and the hooks that always run at fixed moments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A clear way to sort all of this is into two kinds:"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"13.5","title":"What a Harness is Made Of","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/f7c016e83d54bbe365e92558035788a1.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/7c701b6d4a41c179e7c2a228516be579.svg"}},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Guides"}]},{"type":"text","text":" come before the work: instructions, a checklist, an approved plan."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Sensors"}]},{"type":"text","text":" check after the work: tests, a reviewer. What they find goes back to the agent so it can fix it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"And each check is one of two types. Some checks are run by ordinary software, like a form that refuses to submit without a signature: they are fast, cheap and give the same answer every time. Other checks are run by another AI, like a colleague reading the work over: they understand meaning, but they are slower, cost more and can vary. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the fixed, software kind wherever it can do the job"}]},{"type":"text","text":", because that is exactly the guarantee a prompt cannot give you."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"some-actual-examples","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Actual Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"None of these is big:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A sandbox."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The agent works in a separate practice room, with a copy of the files. If it deletes everything by mistake, only the copy is lost."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A permission gate."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Some doors are locked. The agent can try to send money or delete a folder, but it cannot."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A test before \"done\"."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When the agent says it has finished, a check runs. If the check fails, the agent is told it is not done. The agent does not decide that it finished."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A loop detector."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If the agent changes the same file five times, it is probably stuck. Tell it to stop and think again."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"That last one came with numbers. LangChain made five small changes to the surroundings of their coding agent: clearer instructions, a final checklist, a short tour of the project at the start, the loop detector, and more thinking for planning and checking than for routine work. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The model did not change."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Its score on a standard test (Terminal Bench 2.0) went from 52.8% to 66.5%."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Remember that number. It is the reason this module exists: nearly fourteen points came only from changing the surroundings."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"no-harness-is-best-for-every-model","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"No Harness is Best for Every Model"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Take one model, give it one set of tasks, and change only the harness. The scores move a lot."}]},{"type":"image","number":"13.6","title":"DeepSeek V4 Flash across eight harnesses","note":"One model, one set of tasks, eight harnesses, and the scores go from 14 to 20 out of 30. The same model does the thinking in every bar. The fastest harness was also the most expensive per success.","src":"course-images/intermediate/harness-comparison.webp","alt":"DeepSeek V4 Flash across eight harnesses","width":1183,"height":660},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Composio ran one model through eight harnesses, including Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Hermes Agent. The lesson is not \"use the winner\". It is that "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the pairing matters"}]},{"type":"text","text":", like a t-shirt: there is no single size that fits everybody. Claude Code is tuned for Claude models, and Codex for OpenAI's. So when you read that a model is \"the best\", ask: in which harness?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-harnesses-are-open-now","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Harnesses are Open Now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Many harnesses are open source now, including Claude Code's. So a company can take one that works and change the parts that do not fit its job: the instructions, a tool description, or the model inside."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-deterministic"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the same input can give a different answer each time."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness"}]},{"type":"text","text":": everything built around the model that makes it work safely: Agent = Model + Harness."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": designing those surroundings."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Guides"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"sensors"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what the agent is told before it acts, and what checks the work after."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Sandbox"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a separate practice area where mistakes cannot reach your real files."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Permission gate"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a rule that blocks an action, whatever the AI decides."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An AI is non-deterministic, so instructions get you a good success rate but never a guarantee. The harness is the part that does not depend on the AI obeying: the sandbox, the permission gates, the hooks, and the checks that run after the work. The system prompt and AGENTS.md are guides, so they are still advice. Agent = Model + Harness. Changing only the harness moved one agent from 52.8% to 66.5%, and the same model scored from 14 to 20 out of 30 across eight harnesses. There is no best harness, only a best match."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Next: so far a person still sits in the driver's seat. The next module replaces that person."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": An instruction in AGENTS.md and a hook can both stop an agent from touching a file. Why is only one of them a guarantee? And what did the 52.8% to 66.5% jump change?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-articles","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"📄 Articles"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://medium.com/@amirkiarafiei/harness-engineering-what-it-is-and-how-it-complements-context-engineering-6545b40bfc84"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness Engineering: What It Is and How It Complements Context Engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the car, the track and the barriers, in full"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.langchain.com/blog/the-anatomy-of-an-agent-harness"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Anatomy of an Agent Harness"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Agent = Model + Harness, and the list of parts"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.langchain.com/blog/improving-deep-agents-with-harness-engineering"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Improving Deep Agents with harness engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the five changes and the jump from 52.8% to 66.5%"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://composio.dev/content/best-agent-harness-deepseek-v4-flash"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Finding the Best Harness for DeepSeek V4 Flash"}]},{"type":"text","text":": eight harnesses and one model"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-videos","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🎬 Videos"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://youtube.com/shorts/IVdJj_aNwhE"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent Harness Explained in 2 minutes"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the short version, if you prefer to watch"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":[{"question":"An agent must never push to main. Why is the instruction \"do not push to main\" not enough for this rule?","options":["The model does not read the instructions in AGENTS.md.","The instruction uses too much space in the context window.","The model is non-deterministic, so an instruction gives no guarantee.","The model follows instructions only in the first turn."],"answer":2,"explain":"The same input can give a different result next time. An instruction works most of the time, but this rule needs a mechanical part that acts the same every run."},{"question":"How does the harness relate to prompt engineering and context engineering?","options":["The harness is the outer layer. It contains your prompt and context work.","The harness replaces them. You use it instead of prompt and context work.","The harness is a part of the context. It sits inside the context window.","The harness is a new name for context engineering. They are the same thing."],"answer":0,"explain":"Each layer contains the one inside it, so the three are not alternatives. You do context engineering inside the harness you chose."},{"question":"Böckeler splits a harness into guides and sensors. What is the difference?","options":["Guides report how the work went. Sensors tell the agent what to do before it acts.","Guides tell the agent what to do before it acts. Sensors report how the work went.","Guides are written by the vendor. Sensors are written by the user of the agent.","Guides change the model weights. Sensors change the size of the context window."],"answer":1,"explain":"Guides, such as AGENTS.md and tool descriptions, come before the work. Sensors, such as tests and linters, report after the work, so the agent can fix what it broke."},{"question":"LangChain made five changes to the harness of their coding agent. What was the result on Terminal Bench 2.0?","options":["The score increased, because they also used a larger model.","The score did not change, because only the model controls the score.","The score decreased, because more hooks make the agent slower.","The score increased from 52.8% to 66.5%, and the model did not change."],"answer":3,"explain":"The model weights were the same in both runs. Nearly fourteen points came from changes to the environment around the model."},{"question":"Composio ran one model through eight harnesses on the same tasks. What is the main lesson?","options":["Pi Agent scored highest, so every team should use Pi Agent.","The harness has little effect, because the model was the same.","The pairing matters: a harness fits the model it was built for.","The fastest harness is always the cheapest harness per success."],"answer":2,"explain":"A harness makes assumptions about the model it was built for, so another model can do worse in it. Pi Agent won here, but the lesson is the pairing."}]}